	<h2>What I work on</h2>
	<p>
		At <strong>F5 Networks</strong>, I own and operate a Cortex cluster handling roughly 200M active
		series — leading NGINX-based distributor load balancing, a Consul-to-memberlist migration, and
		zone-aware replication rollouts, all with zero-downtime production upgrades. I also build reusable
		Terraform modules for provisioning Global Controller infrastructure, maintain a Go-based Platform
		Manager that automates Kubernetes provisioning across 1000+ customer edge locations, and work on
		etcd-to-PostgreSQL migrations for data replication across Points of Presence.
	</p>
	<p>
		Before F5, I worked as an SRE at <strong>VMware</strong>, <strong>Aqfer</strong>, and
		<strong>IBM</strong> — running multi-tenant Kubernetes platforms, scaling Go data-processing
		frameworks to ingest 13B records per day, managing AWS data lakes, and building out logging and
		automation infrastructure across hundreds of machines.
	</p>

